            "text": "{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CfBmdjwwsWHeWZwH8cGQj\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Bingley's letter, as Caroline frames it, is doing two things at once: reporting Georgiana's charms and planting the idea of her as Bingley's intended. The \\\"hope we dare to entertain\\\" is Caroline's hope, not her brother's — the admiration she attributes to him is thin (\\\"admires her greatly already\\\"), and the real force lies in \\\"frequent opportunity,\\\" which is simply Caroline arranging that he be kept away from Jane.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3248,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":3248,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":144,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\"}}"
